ee of $2.5M ranks in the above the sector median among Energy peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $23K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["SM Energy Company is a mid-cap energy business with a $7.7B market cap on $3.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 24% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 14-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 5.8\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.3%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 16% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Valued at a 43% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","33 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Energy peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Among the least levered in Energy \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"SM Energy (NYSE:SM) Stock Crosses Above 200 Day Moving Average \u2013 What\u2019s Next?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/sm-energy-nysesm-stock-crosses-above-200-day-moving-average-whats-next.html","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794614475.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.926,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Talos Energy, SM Energy, ProPetro, Peabody Energy, and Riley Exploration Permian stocks trade up, what you need to know","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nyse/talo/news/why-up-down/talos-energy-sm-energy-propetro-peabody-energy-and-riley-exploration-permian-stocks-trade-up-what-you-need-to-know","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794515440.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.832,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"SM Nursing and ExamSoft by 